## Audit / gate posture

- Audits are evidence-based against live staging/`next.` + git tip; do not claim GO if deploy ≠ commit, ops unverified, or DB down.
- npm audit: safe patch OK (e.g. Next 15.5.28); **do not** `npm audit fix --force` (Next 16 / zod 4) on cutover day.
- Remaining GO blockers for real production cutover: backups, formal smoke logged, env (`AUTH_*`, Postgres not public), Cloudflare Full (strict), and clean CF cache policy — see `LAUNCH.md` / cutover docs.
- DNS cutover to apex must not happen until a clean release artifact + ops checklist; leave public DNS on current site until then.

## Agent operating habits for this project

- Prefer absolute paths; PowerShell (no bash `&&` / heredoc assumptions).
- After public-ux / `site.js` / `next.config` changes: rebuild UAT and verify both `127.0.0.1:3100` and `https://next.gabbamedicalcentre.com.au` when that environment is in scope.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env`, or dirty laptop-only deploys; ship from a known git SHA.
- `uat:build` may rewrite `apps/web/next-env.d.ts` to `.next-uat/types` — restore to `.next/types` before commit if dirty.
- Never start Phase B implementation unless the user prompt explicitly names a B-task.
